From b4599e950a9cab700f7ff63451a5287184cfbf10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 11:17:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06802/11362] Confirm wa30 L2 80-move bound exact; settle the
 line (v8 probe)

v8 tested the last open hypothesis (turn-vs-move cost split): direction
changes across continue-straight, 180-degree, and 90-degree scenarios
all bundled the reorientation and translation into a single
timer-costing action -- no separate free/costly turn-only step exists.
This confirms the v5 optimistic 80-move lower bound is exact, not an
under- or overestimate. Combined with v6/v7 (multi-carry, ACTION6/
diagonal, and push all refuted), all four follow-up hypotheses tested
across attempts 5-8 are exhausted. wa30 L2 is now a fully settled dead
end for this project's live-agent mechanics under everything testable
via legitimate interactive discovery -- logged to the registry so a
future session doesn't re-run the same four probes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
---
 ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml b/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml
index 3995bc37a7..7ed6537bc0 100644
--- a/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml
+++ b/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml
@@ -875,6 +875,20 @@ games:
     restructured to avoid redundant re-orientations the current 80-move Manhattan
     model implicitly charges for). Absent that, wa30 L2 should be treated as a
     confirmed dead end for this project''s live-agent mechanics.'
+  - 'v8 (results/outer_loop_gpt56sol_wa30_probe_v8.json): tested the last remaining
+    hypothesis directly -- issued ACTION1-4 across multiple direction-change
+    scenarios (continue-straight, 180-degree reversal, 90-degree turn) and compared
+    player grid-cell deltas against timer deltas for each. Every unobstructed
+    direction-change press translated the player one cell AND consumed exactly one
+    timer tick in the SAME call -- no separate stationary turn-only press exists;
+    turn and move are bundled. CONFIRMED (not refuted, not worse): the 80-move
+    optimistic lower bound is exactly correct as originally computed. wa30 L2 is now
+    a FULLY SETTLED dead end for one-block-at-a-time cardinal-move carrying -- all
+    four follow-up hypotheses (multi-carry, ACTION6/diagonal, push, turn-vs-move
+    split) across v5-v8 are empirically refuted or confirmed-neutral. No further
+    interaction-mechanic probing is expected to move this; a future attempt would
+    need either an entirely different theory of the puzzle (not yet conceived) or
+    to accept the 4/5-placement ceiling and move effort to a different game.'
 - game: s5i5
   reproducibility: reproduced
